  "final_answer": "## Brief Introduction to The Allrecipes Allstars\n\nI successfully navigated to the Allrecipes website and found the introduction to The Allrecipes Allstars on the Allrecipes community section (linked from the \"About Us\" area). Here is what Allrecipes says about the Allstars:\n\n**Page Title:** *Meet the Allrecipes Allstars: Brand Ambassadors to the World's Largest Food Community* (by Ansley Emmet)\n\n### Introduction to The Allrecipes Allstars:\n\n> **\"The Allrecipes Allstars are the voice of our community.** This group of 70+ passionate home cooks and content creators from across the country knows what works in the kitchen—because they cook every day, just like you. Since 2011, they've shared trusted recipes and practical tips with the more than 60 million people who visit Allrecipes each month.\n>\n> These 10 Allstars offer a snapshot of our community, showcasing its diversity in talent, locations, and cooking styles. Together with the rest of the Allstars, they've developed and photographed 7,000+ recipes, and have left an additional 41,000+ reviews across recipes on our site.\"\n\n### Key Highlights:\n- **Role:** Brand ambassadors and the voice of the Allrecipes community\n- **Size:** A group of 70+ passionate home cooks and content creators from across the United States\n- **Established:** Since 2011\n- **Audience:** More than 60 million people visit Allrecipes each month\n- **Featured spotlight:** 10 Allstars showcased at a time, representing the community's diversity in talent, locations, and cooking styles\n- **Contributions:** Together they've developed and photographed 7,000+ recipes and left over 41,000+ reviews\n\nThe page then introduces individual Allstars such as Lindsey Close (Denver-based food creator), Ramona Cruz-Peters (Texas-based mom and cookbook author), and Shelley Fang (Dallas-based content creator behind @salty_shelley), among others.\n\n**Source:** https://www.allrecipes.com/allstars-8661275",
